     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&#39;trebuchet ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(51,102,102)\">The rainbow palette is generally not recommended (e.g., <a href=\"http://www.research.ibm.com/people/l/lloydt/color/color.HTM\" style=\"font-family:arial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.research.ibm.com/people/l/lloydt/color/color.HTM&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372459756000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0AohUX6KcP_XROkflup374\">http://www.research.ibm.com/people/l/lloydt/color/color.HTM</a>). </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&#39;trebuchet ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(51,102,102)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&#39;trebuchet ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(51,102,102)\">You can make your own colour palette using the colorRampPalette function: <a href=\"http://www.inside-r.org/r-doc/grDevices/colorRampPalette\" style=\"font-family:arial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.inside-r.org/r-doc/grDevices/colorRampPalette&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372459756000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2bWg1DOhQ3VsXt5_SHhpYp\">http://www.inside-r.org/r-doc/grDevices/colorRampPalette</a></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&#39;trebuchet ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(51,102,102)\">Here are some example colour schemes <a href=\"http://geography.uoregon.edu/datagraphics/color_scales.htm\" style=\"font-family:arial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://geography.uoregon.edu/datagraphics/color_scales.htm&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372459756000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3bs4zQEPCm8SSgWlKX_BbK\">http://geography.uoregon.edu/datagraphics/color_scales.htm</a>.</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&#39;trebuchet ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(51,102,102)\">RColorBrewer has some built in colour schemes you can use to create palettes: <a href=\"http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/RColorBrewer/RColorBrewer.pdf\" style=\"font-family:arial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/RColorBrewer/RColorBrewer.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372459756000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Njlm4yBIUXzrXN2y0uNZB\">http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/RColorBrewer/RColorBrewer.pdf</a></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&#39;trebuchet ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(51,102,102)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&#39;trebuchet ms&#39;,sans-serif;color:rgb(51,102,102)\">\r\n\r\n\r\nNicole</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
